===========================================================================
IMAGES AND OTHER NON-CODE ASSETS
===========================================================================

The entries above cover code. This section records what is known about the
image data that ships with Scidc, and -- just as important -- what is not.
It is a status report, not a claim of clearance.

Where the image data lives
--------------------------
As files in the tree (copied into usr/share/scidc-beta/ when building the
AppImage):

    tcl/textures/       287 images, 22 MB   board and background textures
    tcl/flags/          289 images          country flags
    tcl/help/images/     90 images          figures for the help pages
    tcl/cursor/          41 images          mouse cursors (.xcur, .xbm)
    tcl/images/          36 images          decorative motives, the logo
    freedesktop.org/     36 images          desktop and file type icons
    icons/               12 images          the logo, plus its SVG sources

Embedded as base64 inside Tcl sources -- these do not show up in any file
listing; 1306 images in 47 files, the largest being:

    tcl/utils/countries.tcl   441   the flags again, for the user interface
    tcl/icons.tcl             422   all user interface icons, incl. the logo
    tcl/app-db-icons.tcl      140   database type icons
    tcl/splash.tcl              1   the splash screen

tcl/pieces/ holds 35 piece sets, but no image files: they are SVG paths
written out in Tcl source.

Documented
----------
** Logo and splash screen
Copyright (C) 2026 Mirik -- own work, GNU GPL v2 or later like the rest of
the program. Sources: icons/scidc-logo.svg, icons/scidc-logo-cropped.svg,
icons/scidc-splash.svg; every derived file is generated by
tools/render-icons.tcl. See icons/README.

** Chess piece sets (tcl/pieces/, 35 sets)
Copyright (C) 2009-2013 Gregor Cramer, GNU GPL v2 or later -- all 35 files
carry that header. They are SVG tracings of chess fonts; 20 of them name
the font they follow (Armando H. Marroquin, Eric Bentzen, Colin M. L.
Burnett, David L. Brown, Matthieu Leschemelle, Alastair Scott, Christian
Poisson). The remaining 15 name no source.

** Board themes
Credited in the About dialog to Jose Carlos Martins and Gregor Cramer.

** Country flags
Credited in the About dialog to Mark James (famfamfam.com, public domain)
and Gregor Cramer. See the contradiction noted below.

Not documented
--------------
** Textures (tcl/textures/, 287 files, 22 MB)
No statement of origin anywhere in the tree. File names such as
WoodFine0006_Green.png or Melamine-wood-006.png follow the naming schemes
of commercial texture libraries, whose terms typically forbid redistributing
the raw files. This is the largest single block of redistributed image data
and the one with the least information.

** User interface icons (tcl/icons.tcl and others, ~1300 images)
No designer is named. The About dialog defines a heading for icon design
("Icon design") but never renders it -- there is nobody to credit it to.

** Decorative motives (tcl/images/, "Motive-*.png")
No statement of origin. The files carry no author metadata, only timestamps
and "Adobe ImageReady".

** Mouse cursors (tcl/cursor/)
No statement of origin.

Contradiction to resolve
------------------------
tcl/flags/readme says the flags were "downloaded from
http://addgadget.com/clock/", with fourteen more "found in the internet"
and six drawn by the author. The About dialog credits the same category to
Mark James / famfamfam, whose flag set is public domain. One of the two is
wrong. If it is famfamfam, the flags are clear; if it is addgadget, their
status is unknown. The flags exist twice over -- as files in tcl/flags/ and
embedded in tcl/utils/countries.tcl -- so a replacement would have to touch
both.

Resolved
--------
icons/ formerly held a "Read Me.rtf" stating the icons were "free for
personal non-commercial use". Such a clause cannot be combined into a GPL
work nor shipped in a publicly distributed AppImage. Whether it actually
covered the files present or was left over from Scidb could not be
established, so the artwork was replaced rather than redistributed (version
26.09.17-b2 to b5).
